Subject: [PATCH] docs: add "Single-Node Dev on k3d"

A walkthrough for running the platform on one developer machine through
the existing BYO path (existing_kubernetes) on a k3d cluster: cluster
create flags (Traefik off, host 80/443 mapped through k3d's load
balancer), the global_config.yaml settings that differ on k3s
(metallb_enabled: false for ServiceLB, istio_platform: k3s,
local-path from k3s, best-effort when NRI is unavailable or already
owned), /etc/hosts on loopback, and teardown.

Linked from docs/README.md under Deploy. The page notes the istio and
envoy_gateway changes it depends on.
